{
  "type": "mod",
  "id": 2536,
  "hub_id": null,
  "guid": "com.epicrangetime.blicky",
  "name": "Danger Blicky",
  "slug": "danger-blicky",
  "teaser": "Hey the blicky says not to load coins, but if it's the only weapon you've got...",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/AJYeWcY7WP5o7owsoYHmaDRuwqYRrarPYMRQAYLU.png",
  "downloads": 750,
  "favourites_count": 0,
  "description": "<div class=\"tabset\"><div id=\"tabset-1-panel-1\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Introduction</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p>Hey guys,</p>\n<p>This mod just adds a United States Quarter as ammunition for the blicky.</p>\n<p>It is sold by Peacekeeper at LL2 for 15 roubles.</p>\n<p>There isn’t much more to say about it, have fun!</p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-2\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">How To Install and Compatibility</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p>How to install:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Download the latest release by clicking the button above.</li>\n<li>Open the downloaded zip file with your choice of archive manager (DO NOT USE THE BUILT IN WINDOWS ONE)</li>\n<li>Put the contents of the zip file into your SPT folder</li>\n<li>Enjoy!</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For updates, always delete the previous version of the mod prior to dragging the new version in. Do not overwrite mods when you update! This can leave files in place that can mess with new versions.</p>\n<p>Compatibility:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Most other content mods work with this, report any that don’t.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Incompatibility:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If you are not using a patch for this mod with realism you will have many issues. Either make your own patch or wait for someone to make one. I do not have one.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The standard way to troubleshoot this mod is as follows:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>If you have issues when you install this mod, try making a new profile (preferably a dev bear profile) and make sure your game works. I do this by standard with my mod prior to release anyways, so it should always work.</li>\n<li>Add your previously used mods and boot the game and run a raid after each installed mod. This is to see if anything is conflicting with my mod. Tell me what is conflicting and what your error message is so that I can verify whether it can be fixed or if it just needs to be added to incompatibilities.</li>\n<li>If you are using something that is already listed as an incompatibility I am not going to help you.</li>\n</ol></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-3\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Credits</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p>Many thanks to GrooveypenguinX and CJ for the help getting my codebase together and making it work for me.</p>\n<p>Thank you to Tron for being a constant resource in brainstorming and troubleshooting as I continue to grow.</p>\n<p>Moxopixel for being a wealth of knowledge in the texturing department, I could not have done half of this without seeing what you’ve done.</p>\n<p>Thank you SSH for providing an SDK to streamline the process of creating items.</p>\n<p>Many thanks to my Ko-Fi supporters for the help:</p>\n<p>Bloo</p>\n<p>Ehtacs</p>\n<p>Nazlug</p>\n<p>TwistedTeddy36</p>\n<p>Check out the WTT server <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://discord.gg/hKRbR6yvf2\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">here.  </a></p>\n<p>Support me on Ko-Fi <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://ko-fi.com/epicrangetime\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">here.</a></p></div></div></div>\n",
